IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`
IMPORT `sgba-vintage`

-- Broadcasting Act 1994 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 25 September 2024.
-- LAYER 1, PART 10A, Division 3 (REGULATED ONLINE COMMUNICATION SERVICES, ss 45K to 45O).
-- These rules state the 2024 consolidation (Part 10A entered wef 1 February 2023). The Authority's satisfaction and its choice of amounts and steps are asked as plain facts.

§ `45K. Regulated online communication service`

-- src:3151 | 45K.—(1) The Authority may designate an online communication
-- src:3152 | service with a Singapore end-user link as a regulated online
-- src:3153 | communication service with effect from a date specified in that
-- src:3154 | order if the Authority, after taking into account —
-- src:3156 | (a) the range of all online communication services provided to
-- src:3157 | Singapore end-users; and
-- src:3159 | (b) the extent and nature of the effect that the different types of
-- src:3160 | online communication services have on the people of
-- src:3161 | Singapore and her different communities,
-- src:3163 | is satisfied that the online communication service should be a
-- src:3164 | regulated online communication service in furtherance of the
-- src:3165 | purposes in section 45A.
@ref s 45K(1) (src:3151-3165)
GIVEN `the Authority took into account the range of all online communication services provided to Singapore end-users` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority took into account the extent and nature of the effect that the different types of online communication services have on the people of Singapore and her different communities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority is satisfied that the service should be a regulated online communication service in furtherance of the purposes in section 45A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45K(1) the Authority may designate the online communication service with a Singapore end-user link as a regulated online communication service` MEANS
    `the Authority took into account the range of all online communication services provided to Singapore end-users` AND `the Authority took into account the extent and nature of the effect that the different types of online communication services have on the people of Singapore and her different communities` AND `the Authority is satisfied that the service should be a regulated online communication service in furtherance of the purposes in section 45A`

-- src:3170 | (2) The Authority must cause notice of every designation under
-- src:3171 | subsection (1) to the public by causing it to be published in any other
-- src:3172 | manner that the Authority considers will secure adequate publicity
-- src:3173 | for the designation.
@ref s 45K(2) (src:3170-3173)
GIVEN `the Authority published notice of the designation in a manner that secures adequate publicity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45K(2) the Authority has given the public notice of the designation as the subsection requires` MEANS
    `the Authority published notice of the designation in a manner that secures adequate publicity`

-- src:3175 | (3) A designation under subsection (1) may be revoked at any time
-- src:3176 | by the Authority by instrument in writing; and the Authority must
-- src:3177 | give notice, or cause the giving of notice, of the revocation in the
-- src:3178 | same manner in which the designation was first given.
@ref s 45K(3) (src:3175-3178)
GIVEN `the Authority revoked the designation by instrument in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45K(3) the designation is revoked` MEANS
    `the Authority revoked the designation by instrument in writing`

-- src:3180 | (4) To avoid doubt, the non-publication of any notice of a
-- src:3181 | designation under subsection (1), or its revocation, in the manner
-- src:3182 | described in subsection (2) does not affect the validity of the
-- src:3183 | designation or revocation, as the case may be.
@ref s 45K(4) (src:3180-3183)
GIVEN `the notice of the designation or its revocation was not published in the manner described in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45K(4) the validity of the designation or revocation is affected` MEANS
    IF `the notice of the designation or its revocation was not published in the manner described in subsection (2)` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§ `45L. Online Code of Practice for regulated online communication service`

-- src:3190 | 45L.—(1) Without limiting section 6, the Authority may, from time
-- src:3191 | to time and in accordance with rules made under subsection (2) —
-- src:3193 | (a) issue one or more online Codes of Practice applicable to
-- src:3194 | providers of any regulated online communication service
-- src:3195 | or specified types of such providers; and
-- src:3197 | (b) amend or revoke any online Code of Practice issued under
-- src:3198 | paragraph (a),
-- src:3200 | with respect to all or any of the matters in subsection (4) relating to
-- src:3201 | the provision of that regulated online communication service.
@ref s 45L(1) (src:3190-3201)
GIVEN `it is issued, amended or revoked in accordance with the rules made under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45L(1) the Authority may issue, amend or revoke an online Code of Practice applicable to providers of a regulated online communication service` MEANS
    `it is issued, amended or revoked in accordance with the rules made under subsection (2)`

-- src:3203 | (2) The Minister may make rules prescribing the manner or form of
-- src:3204 | procedure to be followed in connection with the preparation and
-- src:3205 | issuing of online Codes of Practice applicable to providers of
-- src:3206 | regulated online communication services, and any amendment or
-- src:3207 | revocation of any such Code of Practice, including rules requiring the
-- src:3208 | Authority —
-- src:3210 | (a) to give prior notice of any draft online Code of Practice
-- src:3211 | proposed to apply to providers of any regulated online
-- src:3212 | communication service or particular regulated online
-- src:3213 | communication service (including a draft Code of
-- src:3218 | Practice that is to replace an online Code of Practice in
-- src:3219 | force) or any proposal of amendments to or revocation of
-- src:3220 | an online Code of Practice in force;
-- src:3222 | (b) to specify the place or places where copies of any draft
-- src:3223 | online Code of Practice or the proposed amendment or
-- src:3224 | revocation may be inspected;
-- src:3226 | (c) to invite objections and representations in connection with
-- src:3227 | the draft online Code of Practice or the proposed
-- src:3228 | amendment or revocation; and
-- src:3230 | (d) to consider or inquire into all or any of those objections and
-- src:3231 | representations where made in accordance with the rules.
@ref s 45L(2) (src:3203-3231)
GIVEN `the Minister has made rules prescribing the procedure for the preparation and issuing of online Codes of Practice, including prior notice, places of inspection, an invitation of objections and representations, and a duty to consider them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45L(2) the Minister's rules govern the procedure` MEANS
    `the Minister has made rules prescribing the procedure for the preparation and issuing of online Codes of Practice, including prior notice, places of inspection, an invitation of objections and representations, and a duty to consider them`

-- src:3233 | (3) If any provision in any online Code of Practice issued or
-- src:3234 | amended under subsection (1) is inconsistent with any provision of
-- src:3235 | this Act or the Part 10A regulations, that provision in that Code —
-- src:3237 | (a) is to have effect subject to this Act and the Part 10A
-- src:3238 | regulations; or
-- src:3240 | (b) having regard to the provisions of this Act and the Part 10A
-- src:3241 | regulations, does not have effect.
@ref s 45L(3) (src:3233-3241)
GIVEN `a provision of the Code is inconsistent with a provision of this Act or the Part 10A regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45L(3) the provision of the Code has effect subject to this Act and the Part 10A regulations, or has no effect` MEANS
    IF `a provision of the Code is inconsistent with a provision of this Act or the Part 10A regulations` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3243 | (4) An online Code of Practice issued or amended under this section
-- src:3244 | applicable to providers of any regulated online communication
-- src:3245 | service or specified types of such providers may provide for all or any
-- src:3246 | of the following:
-- src:3248 | (a) requirements that a provider of the regulated online
-- src:3249 | communication service must, by establishing and
-- src:3250 | applying appropriate systems or processes, provide the
-- src:3251 | service in a way that —
-- src:3253 | (i) prevents Singapore end-users of its service
-- src:3254 | (particularly children of different age groups) from
-- src:3255 | accessing content that presents a material risk of
-- src:3256 | significant harm to them; and
-- src:3258 | (ii) mitigates and manages the risks of danger to
-- src:3259 | Singapore end-users of its service (particularly
-- src:3260 | children of different age groups) from content
-- src:3261 | provided or that may be provided on its service;
-- src:3266 | (b) any matter so as to provide practical guidance or certainty
-- src:3267 | in respect of what content does or does not present a
-- src:3268 | material risk of significant harm to Singapore end-users
-- src:3269 | generally or certain types of Singapore end-users of the
-- src:3270 | service;
@ref s 45L(4)(a) and (b) (src:3243-3270)
GIVEN `it requires the provider, by appropriate systems or processes, to prevent Singapore end-users (particularly children) from accessing content presenting a material risk of significant harm, and to mitigate and manage risks of danger to them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it provides practical guidance or certainty on what content does or does not present a material risk of significant harm` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45L(4) the Code may provide for this` MEANS
    IF `it requires the provider, by appropriate systems or processes, to prevent Singapore end-users (particularly children) from accessing content presenting a material risk of significant harm, and to mitigate and manage risks of danger to them` OR `it provides practical guidance or certainty on what content does or does not present a material risk of significant harm` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3272 | (c) the procedures to be followed by a provider of the
-- src:3273 | regulated online communication service so as to satisfy
-- src:3274 | the duty under section 45M to comply with the online Code
-- src:3275 | of Practice applicable to that provider, which may
-- src:3276 | include —
-- src:3278 | (i) undergoing (at its own cost) such audit as the
-- src:3279 | Authority may require to ascertain the provider’s
-- src:3280 | compliance with the provisions of the online Code of
-- src:3281 | Practice applicable to the provider;
-- src:3283 | (ii) reporting to the Authority, periodically or whenever
-- src:3284 | requested by the Authority, information about the
-- src:3285 | measures taken by the provider to ensure that
-- src:3286 | Singapore end-users are able to use the regulated
-- src:3287 | online communication service in a safe manner; or
-- src:3289 | (iii) conducting risk assessments on the systemic risks
-- src:3290 | brought about by or relating to the functioning and
-- src:3291 | use of their services and taking reasonable and
-- src:3292 | effective measures aimed at mitigating those risks;
@ref s 45L(4)(c) (src:3272-3292)
GIVEN `it requires the provider to undergo, at its own cost, an audit the Authority requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it requires the provider to report to the Authority, periodically or on request, on measures taken to ensure Singapore end-users can use the service safely` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it requires the provider to conduct risk assessments on systemic risks and take reasonable and effective mitigating measures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45L(4)(c) the Code may include this procedure for satisfying the duty under section 45M` MEANS
    IF `it requires the provider to undergo, at its own cost, an audit the Authority requires` OR `it requires the provider to report to the Authority, periodically or on request, on measures taken to ensure Singapore end-users can use the service safely` OR `it requires the provider to conduct risk assessments on systemic risks and take reasonable and effective mitigating measures` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3294 | (d) a requirement for collaboration or cooperation by the
-- src:3295 | provider of the regulated online communication service
-- src:3296 | with any conduct of research into its regulated online
-- src:3297 | communication service by a suitable expert or experts
-- src:3298 | approved by the Authority, so as to assist in developing the
-- src:3299 | Authority’s understanding of —
-- src:3301 | (i) the nature and level of the systemic risks brought
-- src:3302 | about by or relating to the functioning and use of the
-- src:3303 | regulated online communication service; and
-- src:3305 | (ii) the evolution and severity of such online systemic
-- src:3306 | risks;
-- src:3311 | (e) any matter that promotes or furthers any purpose in
-- src:3312 | section 45A.
@ref s 45L(4)(d) and (e) (src:3294-3312)
GIVEN `it requires the provider to collaborate or cooperate with research into its service by experts approved by the Authority, to help understand the nature, level, evolution and severity of systemic risks` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is any matter that promotes or furthers a purpose in section 45A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45L(4) the Code may also provide for this` MEANS
    IF `it requires the provider to collaborate or cooperate with research into its service by experts approved by the Authority, to help understand the nature, level, evolution and severity of systemic risks` OR `it is any matter that promotes or furthers a purpose in section 45A` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `45M. Duty of regulated online communication service provider`

-- src:3318 | 45M.—(1) Every provider of a regulated online communication
-- src:3319 | service has the duty to take all reasonably practicable steps to comply
-- src:3320 | with the online Code of Practice applicable to the provider in the
-- src:3321 | provision of the regulated online communication service.
@ref s 45M(1) (src:3318-3321)
GIVEN `the provider took all reasonably practicable steps to comply with the online Code of Practice applicable to it in the provision of the service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45M(1) the provider has done its duty` MEANS
    `the provider took all reasonably practicable steps to comply with the online Code of Practice applicable to it in the provision of the service`

-- src:3323 | (2) Where it is alleged for the purposes of this Act that any provider
-- src:3324 | of a regulated online communication service failed to comply with
-- src:3325 | the duty under subsection (1), it is for the provider to show that —
-- src:3327 | (a) it was not reasonably practicable to do more than what was
-- src:3328 | in fact done to satisfy that duty; and
-- src:3330 | (b) there was no better practicable means than was in fact used
-- src:3331 | to satisfy that duty.
@ref s 45M(2) (src:3323-3331)
-- Where a failure is alleged, the burden is the provider's to show both limbs.
GIVEN `the provider shows it was not reasonably practicable to do more than what was in fact done` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider shows there was no better practicable means than was in fact used` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45M(2) the provider has shown what the subsection requires` MEANS
    `the provider shows it was not reasonably practicable to do more than what was in fact done` AND `the provider shows there was no better practicable means than was in fact used`

-- src:3333 | (3) A requirement of an online Code of Practice applicable to a
-- src:3334 | provider of a regulated online communication service has effect
-- src:3335 | despite —
-- src:3337 | (a) any duty of confidentiality or privacy imposed by any rule
-- src:3338 | of law; or
-- src:3340 | (b) any duty imposed by any contract or any rule of
-- src:3341 | professional conduct,
-- src:3343 | that prevents the provider from complying with that requirement or
-- src:3344 | restricts the provider in such compliance.
@ref s 45M(3) (src:3333-3344)
GIVEN `a duty of confidentiality or privacy imposed by a rule of law, or a duty imposed by a contract or a rule of professional conduct, prevents or restricts compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45M(3) the requirement of the online Code of Practice has effect despite that duty` MEANS
    IF `a duty of confidentiality or privacy imposed by a rule of law, or a duty imposed by a contract or a rule of professional conduct, prevents or restricts compliance` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3346 | (4) No civil or criminal liability is incurred by a provider of a
-- src:3347 | regulated online communication service or an officer, employee or
-- src:3348 | agent of such a provider, for doing or omitting to do any act, if the act
-- src:3349 | is done or omitted to be done with reasonable care and in good faith
-- src:3350 | and for the purpose of complying with or giving effect to a
-- src:3351 | requirement of the online Code of Practice.
@ref s 45M(4) (src:3346-3351)
GIVEN `the act was done or omitted with reasonable care and in good faith and for the purpose of complying with or giving effect to a requirement of the online Code of Practice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45M(4) the provider, or its officer, employee or agent, incurs civil or criminal liability for it` MEANS
    IF `the act was done or omitted with reasonable care and in good faith and for the purpose of complying with or giving effect to a requirement of the online Code of Practice` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3353 | (5) An online Code of Practice otherwise does not have legislative
-- src:3354 | effect.
@ref s 45M(5) (src:3353-3354)
GIVEN `it is an online Code of Practice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45M(5) the Code has legislative effect, beyond what this Act gives it` MEANS
    FALSE

§ `45N. Regulatory action`

-- src:3363 | 45N.—(1) Subject to section 45O, if the Authority is satisfied that a
-- src:3364 | provider of a regulated online communication service (called in this
-- src:3365 | section and section 45O the defaulting provider) has failed to satisfy
-- src:3366 | the duty under section 45M(1), the Authority may —
-- src:3368 | (a) order the defaulting provider to pay, within a period
-- src:3369 | specified in the order, a financial penalty of any amount
-- src:3370 | that the Authority thinks fit, but not exceeding $1 million;
-- src:3371 | or
-- src:3373 | (b) direct the defaulting provider to take any steps, whether in
-- src:3374 | or outside Singapore, and within a specified time, that may
-- src:3375 | be necessary to remedy the failure.
@ref s 45N(1) (src:3363-3375)
GIVEN `the Authority is satisfied that the provider of a regulated online communication service has failed to satisfy the duty under section 45M(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority has complied with section 45O` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the financial penalty the Authority proposes, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45N(1)(a) the Authority may order the defaulting provider to pay a financial penalty of that amount` MEANS
    `the Authority is satisfied that the provider of a regulated online communication service has failed to satisfy the duty under section 45M(1)` AND `the Authority has complied with section 45O` AND `the amount of the financial penalty the Authority proposes, in dollars` AT MOST 1000000

-- src:3373 | (b) direct the defaulting provider to take any steps, whether in
-- src:3374 | or outside Singapore, and within a specified time, that may
-- src:3375 | be necessary to remedy the failure.
@ref s 45N(1)(b) (src:3373-3375)
GIVEN `the Authority is satisfied that the provider has failed to satisfy the duty under section 45M(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority has complied with section 45O` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45N(1)(b) the Authority may direct the defaulting provider to take the steps necessary to remedy the failure` MEANS
    `the Authority is satisfied that the provider has failed to satisfy the duty under section 45M(1)` AND `the Authority has complied with section 45O`

-- src:3377 | (2) A defaulting provider that does not comply with a direction
-- src:3378 | given to the defaulting provider under subsection (1)(b) shall be
-- src:3379 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:3380 | exceeding $1 million and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a
-- src:3381 | further fine not exceeding $100,000 for every day or part of a day
-- src:3382 | during which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 45N(2) (guilt) (src:3377-3382)
GIVEN `the defaulting provider does not comply with a direction given under subsection (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45N(2) the defaulting provider is guilty of an offence` MEANS `the defaulting provider does not comply with a direction given under subsection (1)(b)`

-- src:3377 | (2) A defaulting provider that does not comply with a direction
-- src:3378 | given to the defaulting provider under subsection (1)(b) shall be
-- src:3379 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:3380 | exceeding $1 million and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a
-- src:3381 | further fine not exceeding $100,000 for every day or part of a day
-- src:3382 | during which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 45N(2) (punishment) (src:3377-3382)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 45N(2) the punishment on conviction` MEANS
    Punishment WITH `fine not exceeding` IS 1000000
                  , `imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is provided`
                  , `daily fine` IS `a further fine not exceeding, per day or part of a day after conviction` 100000
                  , `forfeiture` IS `no forfeiture is provided`

-- src:3384 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2), it is immaterial whether the
-- src:3385 | online communication service concerned is provided from outside
-- src:3386 | Singapore or provided in or from Singapore.
@ref s 45N(3) (src:3384-3386)
GIVEN `the service is provided from outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45N(3) it matters whether the service is provided from outside Singapore or in or from Singapore` MEANS FALSE

§ `45O. Procedure for regulatory action under section 45N`

-- src:3392 | 45O.—(1) Before exercising any powers under section 45N(1) in
-- src:3393 | relation to any defaulting provider of a regulated online
-- src:3394 | communication service, the Authority must give written notice to
-- src:3395 | the defaulting provider —
-- src:3397 | (a) stating that the Authority intends to take regulatory action
-- src:3398 | against the defaulting provider;
-- src:3400 | (b) specifying the type of action in section 45N(1) the
-- src:3401 | Authority proposes to take, and each instance of non-
-- src:3402 | compliance that is the subject of the action; and
-- src:3404 | (c) specifying the time (being at least 14 days from the date of
-- src:3405 | service of notice on the defaulting provider) within which
-- src:3410 | written representations may be made to the Authority with
-- src:3411 | respect to the proposed action.
@ref s 45O(1) (src:3392-3411)
GIVEN `the written notice states that the Authority intends to take regulatory action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies the type of action proposed and each instance of non-compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies a time for written representations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days from the date of service of the notice to the end of that time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45O(1) the notice is the notice the Authority must give before exercising its powers under section 45N(1)` MEANS
    `the written notice states that the Authority intends to take regulatory action` AND `the notice specifies the type of action proposed and each instance of non-compliance` AND `the notice specifies a time for written representations` AND `the days from the date of service of the notice to the end of that time` AT LEAST 14

-- src:3413 | (2) The Authority may, after considering any written representation
-- src:3414 | under subsection (1)(c), decide to take any regulatory action in
-- src:3415 | section 45N(1) that the Authority considers appropriate.
@ref s 45O(2) (src:3413-3415)
GIVEN `the Authority has considered a written representation under subsection (1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45O(2) the Authority may decide to take the regulatory action in section 45N(1) it considers appropriate` MEANS
    `the Authority has considered a written representation under subsection (1)(c)`

-- src:3417 | (3) Where the Authority has made any decision under
-- src:3418 | subsection (2) against any defaulting provider, the Authority must
-- src:3419 | serve on the defaulting provider concerned a notice of its decision.
@ref s 45O(3) (src:3417-3419)
GIVEN `the Authority has made a decision under subsection (2) against the defaulting provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45O(3) the Authority must serve a notice of its decision on the defaulting provider` MEANS
    `the Authority has made a decision under subsection (2) against the defaulting provider`

-- src:3421 | (4) Subject to section 59(2), a decision which is specified in the
-- src:3422 | notice given under subsection (3) takes effect from the date on which
-- src:3423 | that notice is given, or on any other date that may be specified in the
-- src:3424 | decision.
@ref s 45O(4) (src:3421-3424)
-- Subject to s 59(2); the decision takes effect on the date the notice is given or any other date the decision specifies.
GIVEN `the date the notice is given` IS A DATE
      `another date specified in the decision` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 45O(4) the date the decision takes effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER `another date specified in the decision`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date the notice is given`
    WHEN JUST other THEN other
